      "question": "I want to know if Transformer 1 at MAIN is running hot compared with its load. Over the available data window, summarize top-oil temperature (oti), its alarm and trip readings (oti_a, oti_t), and the three phase currents (il1, il2, il3) with neutral current (inut), giving min, max and mean for each. Then tell me whether the highest oti reading happened at the same timestamp as the highest total phase current. Flag any phase whose mean current differs from the other phases' average by more than 10%. If oti has no data, use ati for context and say that the thermal correlation can't be confirmed.",
      "answer": "**Transformer 1 (MAIN): oil temperature against load, 2024-01-15 to 2024-01-19 (5 daily readings)**\n\nThe highest oil temperature does line up with the highest load. But the load barely changes over these five days, so this doesn't show that load is what's driving the temperature.\n\n| Sensor | Min | Max | Mean |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| oti (\u00b0C) | 84 | 87 | 85.4 |\n| oti_a (alarm) | 1 | 2 | 1.8 |\n| oti_t (trip) | 1 | 1 | 1.0 |\n| il1 (A) | 100 | 102 | 100.6 |\n| il2 (A) | 103 | 106 | 104.6 |\n| il3 (A) | 94 | 96 | 95.0 |\n| inut (A) | 5 | 6 | 5.2 |\n\n**Peak oil temperature vs. peak total current:** Yes, they match. The highest oti (87 \u00b0C) was on 2024-01-16, and total phase current also peaked that day at 301 A. On 2024-01-18 the current was also 301 A, but oti was only 86 \u00b0C. Total current stayed between 299 and 301 A the whole time (under 1% variation), so the match is weak evidence of a load-driven temperature rise.\n\n**Phase imbalance (more than 10% from the other two phases' average):** No phase is flagged.\n- il1: 100.6 A against 99.8 A, which is +0.8%.\n- il2: 104.6 A against 97.8 A, which is +7.0%, the highest.\n- il3: 95.0 A against 102.6 A, which is \u22127.4%, the lowest.\n\noti had data for every reading, so I didn't need to fall back on ati.\n\n**Things to check:**\n- **Trip reading:** oti_t is 1 in every record, so the trip is either active or stuck the whole time.\n- **Alarm reading:** oti_a reads 2 in four of five records. That's an unexpected value if the alarm is meant to be a simple on/off flag.\n- **Temperature readings:** Oil is only about 7 \u00b0C above ambient (ati averages 78 \u00b0C, which is very high for ambient). The winding temperature (wti, 79\u201382 \u00b0C) is also below the oil temperature, when windings normally run hotter than the oil.\n\nBefore concluding the transformer is overheating, I'd check the sensor calibration and how the alarm and trip signals are wired.",
      "score": {
