          "generalized_result_verification": true,
          "agent_sequence_correct": true,
          "clarity_and_justification": true,
          "hallucinations": false,
          "suggestions": "The agent correctly targeted Transformer 1 at MAIN, retrieved stats for oti, oti_a, oti_t, il1, il2, il3 and inut (min/max/mean all match the iot.sensor_stats output), pulled iot.history with the relevant sensors to align timestamps, identified the peak-oti timestamp (2024-01-16, 87 \u00b0C) and the peak total-current timestamp (301 A, also 2024-01-16 and again 2024-01-18), and correctly stated they match while appropriately caveating the tiny load variation. The phase-imbalance calculation is arithmetically correct (il1 +0.8%, il2 +7.0%, il3 -7.4%; none exceed 10%). It noted oti had data so ati fallback was unnecessary. The agent skipped explicit iot.stream_extent and iot.installed_sensors calls, but the sensor_stats response already confirmed the 2024-01-15 to 2024-01-19 window and the existing channels, so the essential verification was achieved. For stricter alignment with expected behavior, explicitly calling iot.stream_extent and iot.installed_sensors first would be preferable, and optionally fmsr.assess_load_profile could be used to support the load analysis."
